WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.339
Welcome to our training on how to generate inventory reports in Seller Central.

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:11.910
All sellers with a professional selling account have access to a number of inventory reports for

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.374
their products in the Amazon Store.

00:00:14.374 --> 00:00:19.302
In this video, we'll show you how to access and customize yours.

00:00:19.302 --> 00:00:25.873
You can use inventory reports to see your current quantity levels, SKU-level performance, SKUs that

00:00:25.873 --> 00:00:30.990
are suppressed from Seller Search results, inactive or have quality warnings.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:37.920
To access your inventory reports, open the Seller Central main menu, hover over Reports,

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.560
and select Inventory Reports.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.480
Use the Select Report Type drop-down menu to choose the report

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.940
you'd like to generate.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.320
Below each type, you'll find a summary of what's included in the

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.314
selected report.

00:00:51.314 --> 00:00:57.280
Once you've chosen a report, click customize the columns for this report.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.060
A new page will appear and display additional metrics.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.000
Select a metric from the available attributes

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.925
and click Add to customize the report with that metric.

00:01:07.925 --> 00:01:10.280
To remove the metric, simply select

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.725
it from selected attributes and click Remove.

00:01:12.725 --> 00:01:15.520
Select Save when you're ready to save your

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.401
custom report settings or click Reset to reinstate the default settings.

00:01:20.401 --> 00:01:22.620
Then return to the Inventory

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.416
Reports page and select Request Report to generate your customized report.

00:01:27.416 --> 00:01:29.160
If you'd like to

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:35.040
request a report without making any changes, simply click Request Report after choosing

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.322
the report type.

00:01:36.322 --> 00:01:41.880
Reports are typically generated within 45 minutes, so keep in mind that your

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.606
inventory may change during this interval.

00:01:44.606 --> 00:01:48.240
Use Reports to spot-check your inventory and

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.200
identify trends and compare them against your own records.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.840
You'll find your reports in the

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.126
report status and download columns on the Inventory Reports page.

00:01:59.126 --> 00:02:00.840
After the report is

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.752
generated, the report status column shows ready.

00:02:03.752 --> 00:02:07.080
To download a report, click the download link

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.408
next to it.

00:02:08.408 --> 00:02:14.160
Search Inventory Report in Seller Central to find examples of the metrics included

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.395
in each report.

00:02:15.395 --> 00:02:21.160
You can also find more information about how to manage and update your inventory

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.406
by watching the Managing Your Inventory video in Seller University.

00:02:25.406 --> 00:02:26.680
This concludes our

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.340
training on how to generate inventory reports.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.380
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:32.880
Store!
